AB  - We present PUENYAI, a locally hosted retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) chatbot that answers enquiries on curricula, scholarships, and application procedures using institutional sources. Built entirely from open-source components and deployed on-premises, the system avoids external APIs while keeping answers grounded in official documents. This paper contributes three practical outcomes for higher-education deployments: (i) a reproducible on-prem blueprint—client, backend, embeddings, vector store, and locally served large language model (LLM)—together with the design trade-offs that led to these choices; (ii) a lightweight evaluation protocol (self-queries, structured user tests, and advisor review) that programs can reuse to check relevance, completeness, and policy alignment; and (iii) a set of lessons learned and governance guidelines (coverage of sources, chunking granularity, update workflow, and privacy controls) distilled from implementation. Results observed during formative testing indicate that a compact local stack consistently answers routine enquiries while reducing staff effort; remaining limitations (multilingual handling, admin tooling, and document structure) inform a practical roadmap for campus roll-outs.
