AB  - This paper presents the development of an AIpowered library chatbot system designed to enhance the user experience in academic library services. The system employs a novel hybrid architecture that combines an external API (Gemini 2.5 Flash) for high-performance responses with a local language model (Phi-2) serving as a reliable fallback mechanism. Using a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture, the system provides intelligent book recommendations grounded in the library's MySQL database. User evaluation with 10 participants demonstrated high functional effectiveness with a 93.3% task success rate, though the System Usability Scale (SUS) score of 64.5 indicates opportunities for user experience improvements. Response times averaged 10 – 20 seconds for book recommendations, representing a significant improvement over pure local model implementations. The hybrid approach successfully balances performance, reliability, and data autonomy, providing a practical solution for academic libraries seeking to modernize their services.
