AB  - The Large Language Model (LLM) has shown significant progress in dialogue, reasoning, and knowledge retention capabilities with its powerful natural language processing capabilities, versatility, and flexibility. In depth analysis and research of big data, mining and applying the intrinsic value of big language models, can provide strong technical support for fire protection work and have very high practical significance. The article addresses the issues of insufficient factual accuracy, knowledge updating difficulties, and a lack of high-quality domain datasets that big language models still face when dealing with knowledge intensive tasks in the fire protection field. By introducing an improved Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) strategy, which combines a hybrid retrieval strategy and a fine tuned generative model, it provides more efficient knowledge capture and updating capabilities. Based on in-depth analysis of existing methods, a new framework called HS-RAG (Hybrid Strategy Driven Retrieval Augmented Generation) is proposed, specifically designed for knowledge question answering tasks in the field of fire investigation. The HS-RAG framework consists of three stages: data preparation, model fine-tuning, and retrieval inference. The data preparation stage includes document conversion, metadata extraction and enhancement, and document parsing modules. With the help of metadata extraction and enhancement, efficient indexing and structured processing of fire investigation standard documents are ensured.
