AB  - Fast and accurate symptom screening is a central need to proactive and convenient healthcare provision, especially in distant and resource-limited conditions. Current symptom checker applications and independent conversational agents have weaknesses of limited contextual accuracy, intermittent clinical accuracy, and hallucinating responses, limiting their usefulness in practice. In this paper, the suggested framework is SYMPTOTRACK-AI, a hybrid Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)-based conversational paradigm of intelligent symptom monitoring and initial clinical decision support. The suggested system combines systematic symptom value jointly, longitudinal patient context modeling, medical knowledge search through reputable sources and regulated generative reason to give clinically founded and risk-conscious answers. Triage and safety control module: Dedicated triage and safety control module will guarantee a conservative escalation of the high-risk cases, and self-care advice of the low-risk cases. Experimental testing proves that SYMPTOTRACK-AI is more diagnostic, has a significantly lower incidence of hallucinations, and better triage than rule-based, machine learning-based, and LLM-only symptom monitoring systems. The findings demonstrate the suitability of hybrid RAG structures to improve reliability, safety and user confidence on real-world digital healthcare services.
