AB  - As one of the most disruptive forms of AI, Generative AI and Large Language Models (LLM) have generated groundbreaking applications. One of these applications is Conversational AI or Question-Answering (QA) Systems, where LLMs generate fast and human-like responses to user queries. However, these responses may lack reproducibility and be factually incorrect. This is particularly experienced in domain-specific cases where LLMs need to respond in knowledge areas beyond their foundational training. With the widespread use of these systems, evaluation of their output has become extremely important. However, the development of a robust evaluation method for LLM outputs remains a challenging task. LLM answers in QA systems need to be evaluated on correctness as well as on alignment with the intent of the query. Traditional token-based Natural Language Processing (NLP) metrics are severely inadequate for this task. Ground Truth Answers, or LLM themselves, are used for evaluation. However, these methods do come with limitations in terms of lack of scalability and cost & time constraints. They are suitable for ranking LLMs, but not for evaluating every answer they generate. The present work attempts to develop a real-time Quality Indicator for LLM answers, which does not use ground truth answers or LLM, can be developed in general-purpose programming languages, involves no additional cost, and is easy to interpret. Current work focuses on QA systems, but the idea can be extended to other LLM applications, too.
ER  - 

