AB  - The rapid expansion of Large Language Models LLMs allows the existence of very intelligent systems that provide financial assistance to anyone. This has the potential of opening up opportunities of individuals receiving personalized financial advice. The following paper is going to discuss the procedure of developing a reliable and explaining financial chatbot using Retrieval-Augmented Generation RAG, and few SQL agents. Our idea does not have problems with financial AI: avoiding hallucinating, providing real-time information, providing advice based on the user data, securing the information belonging to the user, and clarifying the concepts. The system merges both the RAG of the correct answers based on credible financial sources and SQL agents of the direct query of databases. In this manner, it provides contextual advice and protects user data by adhering to the zero-trust security principles. A flexible design, where questions are directed intelligently, multiple checking steps and responsiveness to user requirements are also described. The testing indicates that the system is correct in 96.2 percent of the queries with the error rate being 3.8 percent. It takes less than 1.5 seconds to respond and this is faster and more accurate than other techniques. This architecture preconditions the appearance of AI systems that a user can rely on when prompted to take financial advice.
