AB  - The rapid evolution of artificial intelligence (AI) and natural language processing (NLP) has significantly transformed intelligent question-answering (QA) systems. Leveraging large language models (LLMs) with transformer-based architectures, these systems can comprehend and respond to complex natural language queries with remarkable accuracy, finding applications across various domains, including healthcare, education, and customer support. However, challenges such as factual inconsistencies, hallucinated responses, high computational demands, and domain-specific adaptability persist. To address these issues, hybrid architectures integrating LLMs with external knowledge bases and retrieval mechanisms have emerged, enhancing response accuracy, contextual relevance, and system efficiency. This study delves into the progression of QA systems, highlighting key milestones, persistent challenges, and the impact of hybrid architectures in advancing the field.
