AB  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) enhances the performance of Large Language Models (LLMs) by incorporating relevant external documents. However, the conventional RAG framework often requires modifications to the LLM architecture and additional retraining, which introduces substantial computational overhead and complicates the maintenance of fine-tuning performance across various tasks. To address these challenges, we propose RAG-FIRE (Focused Integration and Refinement of Evidence), a novel plug-and-play component that optimizes the integration of retrieved documents without altering the underlying LLM architecture. Our approach consists of two stages. First, we introduce a relevance-aware document filtering module that reformulates the relevance assessment as a Boolean Question Answering (QA) task. This module effectively filters out irrelevant documents, ensuring that only the most relevant evidence is retained. In the second stage, we present a coherenceenhancing document polishing module, which refines the filtered documents to improve their coherence and better align them with the task's context. This polishing process ensures that the retained documents are not only relevant but also clearly presented. RAGFIRE significantly improves LLM performance across a range of tasks. Furthermore, the component is compatible with various retrievers and generators, making it a versatile and efficient solution for integrating external knowledge into LLMs.
ER  - 

