AB  - Chatbots powered by large language models offer a scalable solution to support multiple sclerosis patients by providing accurate, empathetic, and personalized responses to their questions. By incorporating retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and domain-specific medical data, the chatbot can offer up-to-date and evidence-based guidance. The goal of this paper is to present the development of an AI-driven healthcare solution - a well-optimized chatbot, accessible and reliable as a unique helping hand for multiple sclerosis patients, complementing traditional medical care. The development of a large language model (LLM)-powered chatbot designed specifically to support individuals with multiple sclerosis is presented. The developed chatbot aims to assist users in tracking symptoms, generating pertinent questions for consultations with neurologists, and distinguishing between urgent and non-urgent symptoms. However, the paper also identified several critical challenges that necessitate ongoing oversight, including ensuring medical accuracy and reliability of the chatbot's outputs, addressing ethical concerns related to patient data and decision-making, and maintaining empathetic and contextually appropriate responses.
